* The order in which function definitions enter the program has no
* significance (Programming Guide 1.4), so a caller may precede its callee.
$ENTRY Go {
  = <Outer 'k'>;
}

* Outer is defined before Inner, and Inner before Leaf: every reference is
* forward. A front end that resolved names in one pass would refuse this.
Outer {
  s.X = <Inner s.X>;
}

Inner {
  s.X = <Leaf s.X>;
}

Leaf {
  s.X = s.X;
}
